rules:
- id: rule-workflow-execution-model-compliance
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that runtime-native workflows adhere to the CAS Workflow Execution
    Model, where the Runner handles orchestration and workflows focus exclusively
    on reasoning using supplied context without direct repository scanning.
  title: Rule Workflow Execution Model Compliance
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-pattern-decision-lifecycle-alignment
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires consistent interpretation between pattern maturity (knowledge
    evolution) and decision status (governance lifecycle), ensuring these dimensions
    are not conflated in the Architecture Evolution Map.
  title: Rule Pattern Decision Lifecycle Alignment
- id: rule-patterns-born-as-supporting
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all new patterns to be created as supporting by default to ensure
    they are validated through evidence before potentially being promoted to core
    status.
  title: Rule Patterns Born As Supporting
- id: rule-do-not-merge-across-architectural-layers
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Prohibits the consolidation of patterns across different architectural
    layers to maintain clear separation between governance, execution, contracts,
    and reliability concerns.
  title: Rule Do Not Merge Across Architectural Layers
- id: rule-promotion-requires-evidence
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that pattern promotion to core status must be supported by strong
    evidence from multiple sources or systems to ensure foundational stability.
  title: Rule Promotion Requires Evidence
- id: rule-architecture-work-authority
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Establishes Architecture Work as the authoritative source of architectural
    planning state; generated artifacts must derive status from this registry rather
    than maintaining independent state.
  title: Rule Architecture Work Authority
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-decision-schema-must-be-structured
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces the use of a structured YAML decision schema for all Architecture
    Decision Records (ADR) to enable machine processing and consistent interpretation.
  title: Rule Decision Schema Must Be Structured
- id: rule-shared-knowledge-workspace
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Projects must participate in a shared Knowledge Workspace and are prohibited
    from recreating workspace-level governance structures where global assets already
    exist.
  title: Rule Shared Knowledge Workspace
- id: rule-language-semantic-contract
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Foundational global rule defining semantic contracts for architectural
    artifacts, distinguishing between intent and state, and architect decisions versus
    system state.
  title: Rule Language Semantic Contract
- id: rule-heuristic-patterns-require-signals
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires all patterns derived from heuristics to include at least one linked
    signal as evidence to ensure grounding in observed behavior or insights.
  title: Rule Heuristic Patterns Require Signals
- id: rule-precedence-hierarchy
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: 'Defines the mandatory resolution model for rule conflicts: Global Rules
    > Project Rules > Prompt Rules.'
  title: Rule Precedence Hierarchy
- id: rule-system-proposes-architect-decides
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures human-in-the-loop control by requiring that all system-proposed
    architectural decisions be explicitly accepted, rejected, or deferred by an architect.
  title: Rule System Proposes Architect Decides
- id: rule-generated-artifacts-not-authoritative
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Requires that generated governance artifacts summarize authoritative sources
    and do not store or own primary planning or status information themselves.
  title: Rule Generated Artifacts Not Authoritative
- compliance:
    enabled: true
  id: rule-adr-single-source-of-truth
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Designates Architecture Decision Records (ADR) as the sole source of truth
    for architectural decisions; all other artifacts must be derived from them.
  title: Rule Adr Single Source Of Truth
- id: rule-signal-promotion-criteria
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Defines mandatory criteria (recurrence, impact, reusability, and stability)
    that a signal must satisfy before it can be promoted to a pattern.
  title: Rule Signal Promotion Criteria
- id: rule-decisions-must-be-persisted
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Mandates that all architectural decisions are persisted as structured ADRs
    before they can be reflected in the Architecture Evolution Map or other artifacts.
  title: Rule Decisions Must Be Persisted
- id: rule-decision-status-drives-stage
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Enforces that the lifecycle stage of an item (e.g., DONE) is strictly derived
    from its decision status (e.g., accepted).
  title: Rule Decision Status Drives Stage
- id: rule-aem-consistency-with-decisions
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Ensures that the Architecture Evolution Map remains consistent with and
    does not contradict decisions recorded in ADRs.
  title: Rule Aem Consistency With Decisions
- id: rule-core-patterns-must-be-foundational
  precedence: global
  scope: global
  summary: Restricts core pattern classification to foundational architectural primitives,
    preventing the promotion of specific strategies or implementations to core.
  title: Rule Core Patterns Must Be Foundational
summary:
  global_rules: 19
  project_rules: 0
  total_rules: 19
